      "worked": "Since $1+3^x>0$ for every real $x$, the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$, which is symmetric about zero.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{3^{-x}}{1+3^{-x}}-\\frac12\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{1}{1+3^x}-\\frac12\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{1-3^x}{2(1+3^x)}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\left(\\frac{3^x}{1+3^x}-\\frac12\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
